    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1071">

                <pb facs="0935" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4008: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-28T09:00:00-05:00">August 28, 1940—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. A formal request has been received from the Haitian Government that the
                    American Government consent to an [extension] for 1 year of the accord of July 1
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>], 1939.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d1071-f1"/>
                    Assurances are given that revenues in excess of the amount provided in the
                    current budget will be applied for the amortization of the 1922 loan.<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d1071-f2"/> It is further requested that the Haitian
                    Government be relieved of the token payment of 100,000 gourdes provided in the
                    1938 Accord.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d1071-f3"/> The note with English translation
                    will be forwarded in Friday’s air mail.</p>
                <p>While I believe de la Rue<anchor n="60" xml:id="d1071-f4"/> should remain here,
                    does the Department deem it necessary that he proceed to the United States to
                    obtain the approval of the Foreign Bondholders Protective Council so that a new
                    accord can be negotiated?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sparks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
